> Customizing DMS

this page goes over customizing DMS using the settings menu. because much of the settings menu is either self-explanatory or has good explanations, this serves as a reference for parts that are not immediately obvious.

you can open settings from the bar or by pressing *super+S*

### Personalization

the wallpaper settings can be modified using the wallpaper script (*super+W*).
this changes the set wallpaper. turning on per-mode or per-monitor wallpapers here
will prevent the script from working properly.

for color settings, colors are derived from the top section of theme and colors.
auto uses matugen (Material You color generation), different templates give different
results for colors - it's recommended to play around with each.

matugen templates are used to apply the color scheme to other programs.
DMS comes with templates for many applications including:
agents (ags), fuzzel, GTK3, GTK4, Hyprland, KDE, and 58+ templates via InioX:
alacritty, btop, cava, clipse, dunst, firefox, ghostty, gtk, helix, heroic,
hyprland, hyprwat, kitty, kvantum, labwc, mako, mango, matugen (obt), mcfly,
micro, midnight-discord, neovim, niri, obsidian, opencode, prismlauncher,
pywalfox, qtct, quickshell, rmpc, rofi, spicetify, starship, steam, sway,
telegram, television, terminal-sequences, tmux, vivaldi, wezterm, windows_term,
wine, yazi, zathura, zed, zellij, and more.

all templates are enabled by default, so outside of software that needs manual
configuration (firefox, vesktop and vscode), it should work by default.

instructions for manual themes: https://danklinux.com/docs/dankmaterialshell/application-themes

for vesktop: enable the theme under vencord theme settings, then change your theme
(toggle light mode on/off) to make it update.

if GTK or QT applications are not being themed properly, click the fix button
at the bottom of the themes and colors page.

### Dank Bar

SNAPS-OS comes with 4 pre-configured bars: full top bar, bottom bar, top status bar,
and side bar. you can tweak these however you wish.

### Workspaces

affects the workspaces/tags display in your top bar.

### Keyboard Shortcuts

interacts with your mango config. you can see all current binds, add new ones
(which are saved to ~/.config/mango/dms/binds.conf, including overwrites).

### GTK/QT Theming

GTK and QT theming requirements are pre-installed (adw-gtk-theme, qt6ct-kde).
use the fix button at the bottom of themes page if theming isn't working.

### Vesktop/VSCode Manual Theme

vesktop: enable in vencord theme settings, then toggle theme to refresh.
VSCode/code-oss: may need manual theme enablement.
